1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,968
Your dog doesn't just love you; she calculates your exact emotional fragility every single second.

2
00:00:08,268 --> 00:00:17,340
I clipped the experimental decoder onto Maya's collar, expecting simple barks translated into basic canine needs.

3
00:00:17,640 --> 00:00:25,224
Instead, the tiny speaker on the collar whispered my deepest insecurities in my wife's exact voice.

4
00:00:25,524 --> 00:00:32,004
He needs validation today, Maya's collar murmured while she stared blankly at my trembling hands.

5
00:00:32,304 --> 00:00:39,504
My pulse spiked. The device wasn't reading the dog. It was broadcasting Sarah's programmed desires.

6
00:00:39,804 --> 00:00:47,004
I turned to find my wife standing silently in the hallway, watching us with cold, empty eyes.

7
00:00:47,304 --> 00:00:55,200
She smiled, her expression rigidly rehearsed, exactly like the robotic prompts echoing from the dog.

8
00:00:55,500 --> 00:01:02,244
The collar fell from my numb fingers, clattering loudly against the cold hardwood floorboards.

9
00:01:02,544 --> 00:01:09,888
Maya nudged the blinking gadget toward my feet, repeating the exact phrase Sarah had whispered yesterday.

10
00:01:10,188 --> 00:01:15,108
I thought I owned a loyal pet. Then I realized who was actually domesticated here.
